\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Orthonormal blocks for a marginal precision}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{Choose orthonormal bases of the retained space #{X} and the
eliminated space #{Y} in \ref{fdip-005M}.
Relative to the corresponding inclusions, the blocks have matrix
##{Q=\begin{pmatrix}A&K\\K^{\dagger}&D\end{pmatrix},}
and the retained precision is the Schur complement
#{A-KD^{-1}K^{\dagger}}. For a coordinate selector, order the retained
vertices and then the eliminated vertices. The matrix of #{K} then
has entries #{\langle\delta_v,Q\delta_u\rangle}.}

\p{In those coordinates, Mathlib's
\leanref{Matrix.PosDef.inv} gives positivity of #{D^{-1}}.
The congruence lemma
\leanref{Matrix.PosSemidef.mul_mul_conjTranspose_same},
with its positive semidefinite matrix set to #{D^{-1}} and its
rectangular matrix set to #{K}, gives #{KD^{-1}K^{\dagger}\succeq0}.
These declarations support the positivity steps. The equality
criterion, the subspace equivalences and the graph specialization
are proved in the theorem.}
